@startuml DLP-SIEM-Integration-Sequence

' ============================================================================
' Sequence Diagram: DLP Event Flow to SIEM
' ============================================================================

title DLP Event Integration with Log360Cloud SIEM

actor User
participant "File System" as FS
participant "DLP Agent\n(Minifilter)" as DLPAgent
participant "DLP Engine" as DLPEngine
participant "DataSecurity Plus\nServer" as DSPServer
participant "Syslog Forwarder" as Syslog
participant "Log360 Agent" as Log360Agent
participant "Log360Cloud\nSIEM" as SIEM
participant "SOC Analyst" as Analyst

== File Activity Detection ==

User -> FS: Copy sensitive file to USB
activate FS
FS -> DLPAgent: File operation intercepted
activate DLPAgent
DLPAgent -> DLPAgent: Capture file metadata\n(path, size, hash)

== Policy Evaluation ==

DLPAgent -> DLPEngine: Evaluate against policies
activate DLPEngine
DLPEngine -> DLPEngine: Check DLP rules:\n- Content patterns\n- Device type\n- User permissions
DLPEngine --> DLPAgent: Policy violation detected\n(Action: BLOCK + ALERT)
deactivate DLPEngine

== Local Action ==

DLPAgent -> FS: Block file transfer
DLPAgent -> User: Display notification\n"Transfer blocked by DLP policy"
DLPAgent -> DSPServer: Send DLP event
deactivate DLPAgent
deactivate FS

activate DSPServer
DSPServer -> DSPServer: Store event in local DB
DSPServer -> DSPServer: Generate alert

== SIEM Integration ==

DSPServer -> Syslog: Forward event via Syslog\n(RFC 5424, JSON format)
activate Syslog
Syslog -> Log360Agent: Syslog message\n(TCP/UDP port 514)
deactivate Syslog

activate Log360Agent
Log360Agent -> Log360Agent: Parse Syslog message\n(Extract DLP fields)
Log360Agent -> Log360Agent: Enrich with context:\n- User details\n- Device info\n- Historical data

== Cloud Upload ==

Log360Agent -> SIEM: Upload encrypted event\n(HTTPS/TLS)
activate SIEM
SIEM -> SIEM: Index event
SIEM -> SIEM: Correlate with security events:\n- Check user behavior\n- Check file access history\n- Apply correlation rules

== Correlation & Alerting ==

SIEM -> SIEM: Correlation match:\n"Insider Threat Pattern"
SIEM -> SIEM: Create correlated incident:\n- Confidence: 95%\n- Severity: HIGH

SIEM -> Analyst: Send alert\n(Email/Dashboard)
activate Analyst

== Investigation ==

Analyst -> SIEM: Query related events
SIEM --> Analyst: Return:\n- All DLP events (user)\n- Login events\n- File access patterns\n- USB device history

Analyst -> Analyst: Investigate incident
Analyst -> SIEM: Mark incident as confirmed
Analyst -> DSPServer: Execute response action\n(Block USB devices)

deactivate Analyst
deactivate SIEM
deactivate Log360Agent
deactivate DSPServer

@enduml
